module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Descent
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.RingHom.FaithfullyFlat
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.RingHom.Integral

/-!
# Descent of integrality along faithfully flat ring maps

Let `R → T` be a faithfully flat ring map and let `S` be an `R`-algebra. This file shows that if
`T ⊗[R] S` is an integral `T`-algebra, then `S` is an integral `R`-algebra, and deduces the
corresponding `RingHom.CodescendsAlong` statement.

This is the ring-level content of the fpqc descent of integral morphisms of schemes, Stacks Tag
02L9. It completes the family of descent results of `Mathlib/RingTheory/Finiteness/Descent.lean`
(for `Module.Finite`, `Algebra.FiniteType` and `Algebra.FinitePresentation`) and of
`Mathlib/RingTheory/Etale/Descent.lean` (for smooth, unramified and étale algebras), from which
`Algebra.IsIntegral` is absent.

## Main definitions

No new definitions are introduced.

## Main results

* `Algebra.IsIntegral.of_isIntegral_tensorProduct_of_faithfullyFlat`: integrality of algebras
  descends along faithfully flat base change.
* `RingHom.IsIntegral.codescendsAlong_faithfullyFlat`: the same statement in the form
  `RingHom.CodescendsAlong RingHom.IsIntegral RingHom.FaithfullyFlat`, which is the shape
  consumed by `AlgebraicGeometry.HasAffineProperty.descendsAlong_of_affineAnd`.

## Implementation notes

Integrality is not a finiteness condition on the algebra, so unlike the results cited above it
cannot be descended by exhibiting generators; and the monic polynomial witnessing integrality of
`1 ⊗ₜ x` has coefficients in `T`, so it cannot be descended either. The proof therefore descends
module-finiteness of a single subalgebra. For `x : S` put `A = Algebra.adjoin R {x}`. Flatness of
`T` makes `T ⊗[R] A → T ⊗[R] S` injective
(`Module.Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap`), so `1 ⊗ₜ x` is integral over `T` already
in `T ⊗[R] A` (`isIntegral_algHom_iff`); and `T ⊗[R] A` is generated as a `T`-algebra by that one
element, because `A` is generated over `R` by `x`
(`Algebra.TensorProduct.adjoin_one_tmul_image_eq_top` applied to
`Algebra.adjoin_adjoin_coe_preimage`). A `T`-algebra generated by one integral element is a finite
`T`-module (`IsIntegral.fg_adjoin_singleton`), so `Module.Finite T (T ⊗[R] A)` holds and
`Module.Finite.of_finite_tensorProduct_of_faithfullyFlat` gives `Module.Finite R A`, whence `x` is
integral over `R`.

Only flatness of `T` is used for the injectivity; faithful flatness enters solely through the
module-finiteness descent.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02L9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02L9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03C4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03C4)
-/

@[expose] public section

open TensorProduct

variable {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
  (T : Type*) [CommRing T] [Algebra R T]

/-- If `T` is a faithfully flat `R`-algebra and `T ⊗[R] S` is an integral `T`-algebra, then `S`
is an integral `R`-algebra. -/
theorem Algebra.IsIntegral.of_isIntegral_tensorProduct_of_faithfullyFlat
    [Module.FaithfullyFlat R T] [Algebra.IsIntegral T (T ⊗[R] S)] :
    Algebra.IsIntegral R S := by
  refine ⟨fun x ↦ ?_⟩
  set A := Algebra.adjoin R ({x} : Set S)
  have hxA : x ∈ A := Algebra.self_mem_adjoin_singleton R x
  let φ : T ⊗[R] A →ₐ[T] T ⊗[R] S := Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id T T) A.val
  have hφ : Function.Injective φ :=
    Module.Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap (R := R) (M := T)
      A.val.toLinearMap Subtype.val_injective
  have hyint : IsIntegral T ((1 : T) ⊗ₜ[R] (⟨x, hxA⟩ : A)) :=
    (isIntegral_algHom_iff φ hφ).mp (Algebra.IsIntegral.isIntegral ((1 : T) ⊗ₜ[R] x))
  have hpre : (Subtype.val ⁻¹' ({x} : Set S) : Set A) = {(⟨x, hxA⟩ : A)} := by
    ext y
    simp [Subtype.ext_iff]
  have htop : Algebra.adjoin T ({(1 : T) ⊗ₜ[R] (⟨x, hxA⟩ : A)} : Set (T ⊗[R] A)) = ⊤ := by
    simpa [hpre] using Algebra.TensorProduct.adjoin_one_tmul_image_eq_top (R := R) (A := T)
      (B := A) (Subtype.val ⁻¹' ({x} : Set S)) Algebra.adjoin_adjoin_coe_preimage
  have hfin : Module.Finite T (T ⊗[R] A) :=
    ⟨by simpa only [htop, Algebra.top_toSubmodule] using hyint.fg_adjoin_singleton⟩
  have : Module.Finite R A := .of_finite_tensorProduct_of_faithfullyFlat T
  exact (isIntegral_algHom_iff A.val Subtype.val_injective).mpr
    ((Algebra.IsIntegral.of_finite R A).isIntegral (⟨x, hxA⟩ : A))

/-- Integrality of ring homomorphisms codescends along faithfully flat ring maps: if `R → T` is
faithfully flat and `T → T ⊗[R] S` is integral, then `R → S` is integral. -/
theorem RingHom.IsIntegral.codescendsAlong_faithfullyFlat :
    RingHom.CodescendsAlong RingHom.IsIntegral RingHom.FaithfullyFlat := by
  refine .mk _ RingHom.isIntegral_respectsIso fun R S T _ _ _ _ _ h h' ↦ ?_
  rw [algebraMap_isIntegral_iff] at h' ⊢
  rw [RingHom.faithfullyFlat_algebraMap_iff] at h
  exact .of_isIntegral_tensorProduct_of_faithfullyFlat S

end
